   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 433 of the laws of 1997, amending the public health law and other laws relating to rates of reimbursement paid to hospitals and residential health care facilities, in relation to extending the effectiveness of a portable x-ray demonstration program for medicaid recipients",
    "basePrintNo": "S5551",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5551-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1-b, Chap 433 of 1997",
    "lawSection": "Public Health",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5551\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend chapter 433 of the laws of 1997, amending the public health\nlaw and other laws relating to rates of reimbursement paid to hospitals\nand residential health care facilities, in relation to extending the\neffectiveness of a portable x-ray demonstration program for medicaid\nrecipients\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo extend the expiration date of a demonstration program established\nin 1997 to study the cost effectiveness of Medicaid coverage for\nportable x-ray services until June 30, 2012.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 amends subdivision (b) of section 1-b of chapter 433 of the\nlaws of 1997 to extend the expiration date of the portable x-ray\ndemonstration program from June 30, 2010 to June 30, 2012.\n\nSection 2 amends subdivision (c) of section 1-b of chapter 433 of the\nlaws of 1997 to direct the Department of Health to report to the\nLegislature on the demonstration program by September 1, 2011.\n\nSection 3 states the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nPortable x-ray services are important to the aged, infirm and\nchronically ill citizens of New York State, particularly those who\nare residents of long term care facilities or home bound. If an\nindividual cannot access portable x-ray services when an x-ray is\nordered by an authorized health care practitioner, then the person\nmust be transported by ambulance to a stationary radiological site.\nTransporting individuals by means of ambulance is costly and often\ntraumatizing for the patient. Many states allow for Medicaid\nreimbursement for portable x-ray and diagnostic ultrasound services\nas does the federal\nMedicare program. New York state took a first step by creating a\ndemonstration program to allow portable x-ray providers to directly\nbill Medicaid for services provided to Medicaid recipients in\nresidential health care facilities and intermediate care facilities\nfor persons with developmental disabilities. This legislation\nrequires the Health Department to submit its report due September 1,\n2011.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nA.10607 of 2010. Chapter 149 of the Laws of 2008.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nTo be determined.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n\n",
